You are working in the repo /Users/blef/Work/naolabs/chat (a monorepo; backend is apps/backend, Fastify + tRPC + better-auth). Repo conventions: tabs for indentation, minimal comments, nao is lowercase.

Fix a P2 review issue from PR #1389 in apps/backend/src/auth.ts. Read the file first, especially the `databaseHooks.session.create.after` hook (~line 351-357) which currently does:

	session: {
		create: {
			async after(session) {
				await syncRolesFromSsoGroups(session.userId);
			},
		},
	},

Problem: this hook fires for EVERY session creation regardless of auth provider (email/password, Google, GitHub, GitLab, Microsoft, OIDC). `syncRolesFromSsoGroups` (in apps/backend/src/services/sso-group-mapping.service.ts) then reads the OIDC ID token that was STORED at the user's last OIDC sign-in and re-applies group-mapped roles. So a non-OIDC login re-applies stale OIDC group data, and stale group membership can never be corrected via a password/social login. It also adds needless latency to non-SSO logins.

Fix: only run the sync when the session being created results from an OIDC sign-in. The better-auth database hook signature is `after(session, ctx)` where ctx is the endpoint context (GenericEndpointContext) of the request that created the session. The codebase already has a helper `resolveProviderId(ctx)` in apps/backend/src/utils/utils.ts (reads `ctx?.params?.id ?? ctx?.params?.providerId`), used by the `user.create` hooks in the same file to identify the provider. The OIDC provider id comes from `getOidcProviderId()` (already imported in auth.ts from './services/oidc-auth.service'); there is also `isSocialProviderOidc(providerId)` imported in auth.ts — read apps/backend/src/services/oidc-auth.service.ts to decide which comparison is correct (check how the OIDC plugin registers its callback route and what the ctx params look like — the OIDC integration is via better-auth's genericOAuth or sso plugin in `augmentPluginsWithOidc`; make sure the provider-id extraction actually works for that plugin's callback path, e.g. /oauth2/callback/:providerId).

Implementation: in the session.create.after hook, resolve the provider id from ctx; if it does not correspond to the OIDC provider, skip the sync entirely (return). Keep the await for OIDC sign-ins (roles should be applied before the login completes — that is deliberate). If ctx is undefined (internal session creation), skip.

Do NOT restructure anything else in auth.ts.

Check whether any backend tests cover this hook (search apps/backend/tests for syncRolesFromSsoGroups). If a test exists, update it; if not, don't add one (the hook wiring is hard to unit test in isolation).

Verify types compile for auth.ts (e.g. `npx tsc --noEmit -p apps/backend` from repo root is fine if fast; otherwise rely on your careful reading of the better-auth types in node_modules to confirm the second `ctx` parameter exists on database hook `after`).

In your final response, state exactly what you changed, how you verified the ctx/provider-id extraction is correct for the OIDC callback path (cite the better-auth code you inspected), and any test/typecheck results.
